 "about": "Measured values of an open MEng thesis (Stellenbosch University; not peer reviewed as a journal article is), in the format of thermoml_<id>.json (read by measured_components.ThermoML). Read in the text of the thesis PDF as CORE (core.ac.uk) serves it; the PDF itself refused scripts (CORE: a robot check; the university repository: 403), so a person checks every value against the PDF (AGENTS.md rule 4). Table 8.12: boiling temperatures of pure limonene in a dynamic VLE still at set pressures, P in kPa and T in K as printed; repeated readings at the same pressure are kept as printed. Sample: (R)-limonene, Sigma-Aldrich, CAS 5989-27-5, 98.38 wt % by the author's GC and KF analysis (Table 4.1); one enantiomer serves CHEPTA's limonene (docs/DATA_RULES.md section 3, stereoisomers). Uncertainty: the thesis states +/-0.32 K (expanded, coverage factor 2, encompassing temperature, pressure and analysis effects; section 3.4 and chapter 4); turned into a pressure uncertainty here through the slope of the set, 0.0274 per K between 417.0 and 450.9 K (0.88 %). The author notes limonene degrades in the still after about 8 h (Figure 4.1, Appendix H).",
